+Output: `build/libs/BAROX-VS-v007.jar`. The release workflow uses Java 21 and Gradle 8.12, verifies the compiled JAR entries and publishes the release asset.
 
 ## Scope and test note
 
 Features are local cosmetics, local audio playback and HUD/interface elements. The mod does not alter server state or automate combat/movement. CI compilation and JAR integrity checks are not a substitute for running Minecraft on each launcher/device; an actual in-game test on Android/ZalithLauncher remains to be completed.
+
+## v007 rendering fix
+
+World cosmetics now use Minecraft's depth-tested debug-filled-box render layer and are submitted after entity rendering. The previous debug-quads layer ignores world depth and could allow wing geometry to appear through water and blocks. The player model now writes depth before the wing mesh is drawn, so the shoulder attachment roots are occluded naturally. Ambient cosmetics share the same depth-tested path.
+
+## API selection
+
+Fabric API remains the runtime integration layer. The GUI and HUD are implemented directly in BAROX VS, so Cloth Config / LibGui are not additional runtime requirements. The visual meshes are BAROX-owned geometry and procedural motion; GeckoLib is not bundled just to add unused weight. EMF / ETF are client mods for OptiFine-style custom entity models and textures, not general-purpose APIs required by this renderer.
